# Delivery status

Local only. Do not deploy until the user asks. After each product change, update this rule and `docs/SAQ_PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` section 7.

Done locally: signup profile and password policy; Workspace hidden until login; version rename/delete; per-topic target comparison and live gap feedback; email confirmation when SMTP is set, otherwise a confirm link in the signup popup; optional Google sign-in when credentials exist; version-scoped roles; standards catalog on Workspace (not the dashboard), filtered by category and industry; one Help panel per question; Evidence step with checklist ticks, notes, and files. Evidence rows read “Evidence required:” under the question code, then “Current level” and “Target level”. A checklist level is named once (“To achieve level 2:”) and the lines under it are numbered. Action plan shows effort as S/M/L for the size of the work (stored as Low/Medium/High) and labels the calculated timing When to act (Immediate / Urgent / Planned) on the action plan, dashboard, and report. It suggests effort only when the field is empty, includes the gap in that timing, takes an assignee from collaborators or a typed team name, and labels remarks Next step. Improvement-priority scores are unchanged. Postgres and Adminer are published on 127.0.0.1 only.

Still open:

- Phase 9 — Hide on-prem or cloud-only topics only after applicability tags are reviewed. Tags may exist on scope items; scoring ignores them.
- Help is one collapsed panel per question. Column N is the level description. Column R is evidence expected. Every theme has checklist lines: no level 1 line, one level 2 line, and two level 3 lines. On the Evidence step, questions stay collapsed until opened.
- Real SMTP and Google values stay in env files the user fills. Do not invent them.

A container restart does not pick up source changes. Use `npm run docker:up`.
